{"calculus_ref":"stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md","clause_relations":[{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:allowance","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The governed question is capability fit or a cost claim.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"The activation declares its allowance and how spend will be measured.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:allowance-declared-where-cost-is-governed"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:material-closure","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:seed-set","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:relation-family","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Compute the material closure of the seed set under the relation family on the exact basis; if the closure is not finite and unique, the step returns a gap or refusal and does not guess.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:closure-is-computed-on-exact-basis"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"candidate_ready -> satisfied; refused -> falsified; incomplete -> indeterminate; re_entry_requested -> out_of_frame or invalid_basis.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:maps-to","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:construction-availability-maps-to-core"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:constructor","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"One capable context has sufficient authority and intake.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"It enters directly as constructor; coordination is selected only when material contexts, authority or required independence need it.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:direct-entry-unless-coordination-needed"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:fit-test","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:envelope","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The selected context fits the envelope.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"Activate.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:consequence"},{"literal":"If it does not fit, exactly one of: refine the outer contract into steps whose contexts fit; sequence activations; select another actor whose envelope fits; apply a lawful compression; or return out_of_frame.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:exception"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:projection-records-boundary","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:fit-test-against-envelope"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:grant","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The grant names the operations permitted, the territory that may change, and the decisions reserved to others.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:grant-names-operations-territory-reservations"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:intake","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Declared inputs are acquired by their exact identity; a declared input absent from the actor's materialised view is neither licence to read elsewhere nor evidence that it is absent.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:inputs-acquired-by-exact-identity"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:intake","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A step is activated from an intake sufficient to reconstruct its governing relations without conversation history, commentary or a prior actor's memory.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-actor-change","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:intake-is-sufficient-without-history"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:intake","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The intake names: the selected outcome, admitted prerequisite or experiment it serves; the affected relation set and its invariants; the exact basis and the inputs it may acquire, each by identity and hash or by an input commit; the grant; the conditions that require re-entry at an owning relation; and, where the governed question is capability fit or a cost claim, the allowance and how spend will be measured.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:intake-is-sufficient-without-history","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:intake-names-its-fields"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:step","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:actor","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The actor's internal path within a step is not part of the output and is not governed.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:internal-path-is-not-governed"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:lawful-compression","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A compression is lawful only when it preserves the material distinctions and failure detections the evaluation needs.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:lawful-compression-preserves-distinctions"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:material-closure","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The method does not require proving that no undiscovered material relation exists.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:no-proof-of-no-undiscovered-relation"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-satisfied","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A missing, failed or out-of-scope result returns its own member, never satisfied.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:result-algebra-has-five-members","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:nothing-is-coerced-to-success"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A finite actor realises a selected outer contract through steps; each step's selected context fits the actor's envelope; the actor's internal path within a step is its own.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-selected-outcome","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-actor-change","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-produced-facts-are-not-reacquirable","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-open-world","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-candidate-until-evaluated","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"literal":"Standing: recovered as a composite; the generic statement is reframed from the graph profile's graph functions.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p0-statement"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p5-totality","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p0-statement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-open-world","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p6-statement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"literal":"A step can meet a condition outside its context and cannot report success on one; its result algebra carries indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis as first-class outcomes and its control model names the next move.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:consequence"},{"literal":"Standing: derived.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:derives","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p5-derivation"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p6-justification-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports a claim on a basis; authority permits or disposes within scope.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"Standing: independent. A bounded actor satisfying all else can still take a green label as acceptance.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p6-statement"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The actor of one step need not be the actor of the next; a later actor may re-acquire declared sources but not a prior actor's private memory.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-actor-change"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A step's output is a candidate until evaluated.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-candidate-until-evaluated"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The world is open: a step may meet conditions outside its selected context.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-open-world"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:outcome","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"literal":"P0 presupposes a selected outcome (P2).","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-selected-outcome"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:selected-context","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A projection cannot trim a required member to fit a carrier or budget.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:projection-cannot-trim-required-member"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:selected-context","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Project the closure to the selected context, recording its boundary: the excluded, external, unresolved, translated and invalidation-sensitive seams; material not in the closure stays out; adjacent material does not enter because it exists.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:closure-is-computed-on-exact-basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:projection-records-boundary"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:reference","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The reference's owner, exact selector, authenticity, availability and completeness support the same consuming decision as the body.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"Only then does a reference conserve the relation; an inaccessible or insufficient reference is a residual, not success.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:reference-conserves-under-conditions"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-disposition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-ambiguity-outcome","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-profile-closure","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A declared refinement answers a different question, keeps its own vocabulary and declares a total mapping to the core; no refinement adds a core member.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-satisfied","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-falsified","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-indeterminate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-out-of-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-invalid-basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"One core algebra of exactly these five members serves every evaluation and every step's stop state.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p5-derivation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:result-algebra-has-five-members"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:fit-test","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Silent omission of required material to fit the envelope is never a lawful option.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:fit-test-against-envelope","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:projection-cannot-trim-required-member","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:silent-omission-is-never-a-fit-option"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:step","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a